---
import config from '../config.json';

// The band is the site's EXIT, so it answers the three things a visitor asks at the bottom of a page:
// where do I go next, who is this, and when was this written. What used to sit here was a slogan
// ("Join our Math ∑ Book Community") with a glyph pulsing at 0.5s forever and no links at all — the
// glyph was the second-largest thing on the screen (29.9px), which is exactly what D112 forbids: the
// display step belongs to a screen's locator, never to a punchline. Operator ruling, 2026-11-02: the
// footer is designed entirely, and the pulse goes.
//
// Why there is no button in here: the primary control is an `ink` FILL (DESIGN.md "Buttons"), and an
// ink fill on the ink band is invisible. So paths on the band are named by hue instead — the
// `--color-path-*-on-ink` steps exist for precisely this ("the same four paths on the dark band" — the four
// are the outbound platform steps, calendar / Meetup / Discord / Mobilizon, and an internal link like
// `/chat` or `/schedule` carries no hue at all, it is the band's own text colour; the hue is what marks a
// path that leaves the site, 4.74 meetup / 4.59 discord, asserted in the contrast oracle) — and the band
// gets exactly one dark region, which is what `check:render` counts.
//
// No "Home" link: the serif mark below is the home path, same as in the nav (D100, and the operator
// confirmed the fourth nav link goes too).
const year = new Date().getFullYear();
---

<footer class="bg-ink text-band-text">
  <div class="max-w-screen-xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-10">
    <p class="text-micro uppercase tracking-wide">Where to next</p>

    <!-- Targets are 32px tall (16px line box + py-2), the same accepted shape as the nav links; do not
         shave the pad. `outline-band-text` is the focus ring HERE: gold on ink measures 2.50, which the
         oracle bans, and `ratify-check` fails this file if a gold ring comes back. -->
    <nav
      aria-label="Where to next"
      class="mt-1 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-6 gap-y-2"
    >
      <a
        href='/schedule'
        class='py-2 text-label font-medium hover:text-gold-on-ink hover:underline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-band-text'
      >
        Schedule
      </a>
      <a
        href='/chat'
        class='py-2 text-label font-medium hover:text-gold-on-ink hover:underline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-band-text'
      >
        Community chat
      </a>
      <a
        href={`${config.URLs.meetupGroup}/join`}
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
        class='py-2 text-label font-medium text-path-meetup-on-ink hover:underline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-band-text'
      >
        Join on Meetup
      </a>
      <a
        href={config.URLs.discordInvite}
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
        class='py-2 text-label font-medium text-path-discord-on-ink hover:underline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-band-text'
      >
        Discord
      </a>
    </nav>

    <!-- Identity, not a locator: 16px serif at every width, the same face and size as the nav mark,
         because the club's name is carried by the face (D95/D100). The summand is the club's own glyph,
         set inline at the size of the word beside it, in gold-on-ink (5.80), and NOT read aloud — it is
         punctuation here, not a word. -->
    <p class="mt-8 font-body text-body font-bold">
      <a
        href='/'
        aria-label="Minneapolis Math Book Club, home"
        class='py-1 hover:underline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-band-text'
      >
        Minneapolis Math Book Club <span aria-hidden="true" class="text-gold-on-ink">∑</span>
      </a>
    </p>

    <!-- Small print carries the place and the date, and nothing else: no frequency claim (D92), and the
         old "All rights reserved" boilerplate is gone with the rest of the old band. -->
    <p class="mt-6 text-micro">Minneapolis, Minnesota</p>
    <p class="mt-1 text-micro">&#169; {year} Minneapolis Math Book Club</p>

    <!-- One static line, not a component (round 10 ruling on third-party marks). The site names Meetup and
         Discord in its own type and links out; it no longer paints either company's mark — the Meetup png
         that used to sit in the join card was the most saturated colour on the landing page (0.523% of pixels
         at C 0.226) and it was not ours. Naming a platform is nominative use; borrowing its colour and shape
         to do the naming is what gets a site into an argument. If a mark ever comes back it is the official
         file, unmodified, in clearspace, next to the name it stands for (design/records/0013). -->
    <p class="mt-1 text-micro max-w-measure">
      Meetup and Discord are trademarks of their owners. This site is the club's own — not sponsored or
      endorsed by either.
    </p>
  </div>
</footer>
